{
  "format": "pinmame-harness-scenario",
  "version": 1,
  "notes": "robo_a34 service walk. In Data East alpha Switch Test the Player 1/2 displays print the closed switch's ROM name and the Player 3/4 field its wire code and number; NONE marks an address the ROM names as unfitted. Flipper addresses 15/16 are read by holding the flipper keys, because core_updateSw rewrites them from the flipper column. The discrete Lamp Test prints each lamp's ROM name as Start (matrix 3, held 400 ms; a 150 ms hold is not registered) steps it forward once Green is toggled back to Forward; the automatic Coil Test prints each driver's ROM name with its L/R bank number. Display text is PinMAME's decoded segment text; glyphs its decoder does not map appear as '?'.",
  "watch_switches": [
    -7,
    -6,
    15,
    16
  ],
